Hybrid table retrieval: glossary expansion + relationship-graph filtering

Three changes to a hybrid (dense + BM25) table-catalog search:

1. keyword_index.py — index the per-table "rules" text under the KEYWORD_FIELDS
   knob. It was previously concatenated unconditionally, so the setting could
   not turn it off and the index cache fingerprint did not reflect it.

2. query_prep.py (new) — one-directional, query-side synonym expansion for the
   lexical arms only. The dense arm and the exact-match pin keep the original
   query. Deliberately separate from the abbreviation map, which is applied
   symmetrically to documents and queries and so must hold true synonyms.

3. er_filter.py (new) — read the fused ranking far deeper than it is returned:
   keep the first ER_ANCHOR_N unconditionally, then admit tables from the next
   ER_POOL_N only where the relationship graph joins them to that head. This
   recovers tables that belong in an answer as a join dependency and therefore
   have no text surface for either arm to score.

Knobs (env, read once at import): ER_POOL_N=80, ER_ANCHOR_N=10, ER_EXPAND_N=20.
ER_POOL_N=0 restores a plain top-N cut.

The eval harness is updated to judge pass/fail on the search's actual output
rather than on the union of the raw arms, and to log fractional recall next to
the all-or-nothing verdict.

Table and column names in comments are placeholders.
